From 8053e557d59a0582b0baa197491bbb33b42e1de1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
by: triplecN
Subject: [PATCH 17/20] network hardening: hash headers last, Shunko fixes, index/RPC
 corrections

net_processing: the cheap continuity, connect and claimed-work checks now run
before any RandomX hashing. An unconnecting batch with no low-work sync in
progress is a possible BIP130 announcement and is handled without hashing; a
connecting batch whose claimed work is below the anti-DoS threshold and that is
not full can never start a sync and is ignored. A low-work sync continuation is
still hashed, as HeadersSyncState requires. A 200-header unconnecting replay
now costs 0.00 s instead of several seconds of message-handler time.

net_processing: the perticket rate limit drops silently instead of
Misbehaving, so an honest burst or Tor bunching cannot get the relaying peer
disconnected; tickets are not sent over or accepted from block-relay-only
links.

init: -coinstatsindex is refused with a clear error. The upstream index
computes an unclaimed reward that goes negative on PER payout blocks and aborts
the node at the first payout, again on every restart.

rpc/mempool: Shunko never hands to this node's own address (global ::IsLocal),
reports 'may have been delivered' when the tx bytes were already written, and
the recent-target rotation is unchanged.

shunko: a unix-socket proxy keeps its path (copy the whole Proxy), I2P targets
are refused explicitly (IsTor), and the user agent is fixed.

rpc/mining: getblocktemplate declares coinbasefee, reservoirfee and peroutputs,
rewords coinbasevalue, and no longer advertises transactions/prevblock as
freely mutable. mainnet_smoke now runs with -rpcdoccheck=1 so undeclared keys
fail the suite.

Tests: p2p_dos [8] unconnecting valid headers are not hashed; per_regtest [7]
-coinstatsindex is refused; shunko [5b] a receiver that withholds the pong
reports a possible delivery.
